Subject: a pair's continuation gateways lead by tan(22.5) and cover both diagonals
Upstream-file: pcbnew/router/pns_diff_pair.cpp (DP_GATEWAYS::buildDpContinuation)
Why: after a differential pair is fixed at a waypoint, its next leg starts from
 buildDpContinuation's gateways: the anchor pair, and four "angled" ones that
 extend one member along its direction so the pair can turn 45 degrees at the
 fixed point. The extension was the pitch times sin(22.5) (0.383), or sin(23.5)
 as wiggle room (KiCad #12459's fixme); a 45-degree turn needs the outer member
 to lead by the pitch times tan(22.5) (0.414). With sin the turned members end
 0.978 of the pitch apart, so every angled gateway failed the gap check. And
 the angled gateways were added only when delta.x == delta.y, one of the two
 diagonals: a pair fixed on the other got none. So after any diagonal fix the
 pair could not bend at the fixed point (review PR #11 r3 R3-M2: over a sweep of
 two-waypoint detours off the pads' line, none routed before this patch and 155
 routed joined and clean with it).
 Measured with the test suite: every earlier golden line byte-identical.
Upstream: yes, as the fix for KiCad #12459; not yet proposed.

--- a/pcbnew/router/pns_diff_pair.cpp
+++ b/pcbnew/router/pns_diff_pair.cpp
